preConditionHook:
// EL: dojiCount = CountIF(AbsValue(close - open)
//         <= dojiFraction * (high - low), lookback).
//
// The counted condition is DojiBar's, applied bar by bar. CountIF counts bars
// 0..N-1 INCLUDING the current bar and the counted condition is a true SERIES
// (EL_FEATURES `countif`, VERIFIED) -- every price term shifts with the counted
// bar, which is what this loop does. The terms are prices with real history, so
// no zero-filled variable mirror is needed.
//
// Direction-agnostic: both sides are identical text, and 'few dojis' (Brooks's
// strong-trend sign) is this rule NEGATED, a per-placement toggle.
//
// A product, not a quotient: EasyLanguage raises a runtime divide-by-zero error
// on a zero denominator and a zero-range bar is legal data -- it counts as a
// doji, its body being zero as well.
// The count is an EL numeric variable, so a double here, and it persists across
// bars, so it is reset before the loop.
dojiCount = 0.0;
for (int i = 0; i < (int)lookback; ++i) {
    if (el_le(std::fabs(close[i] - open[i]), dojiFraction * (high[i] - low[i]))) {
        dojiCount = dojiCount + 1;
    }
}
